{"title":"Coral Pharmacy","sub":"Four warehouses into one?","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Retail pharmacy","geo":"Australia","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Network design · risk pooling · trade-offs","prompt":"Coral runs 600 pharmacies across eastern Australia, supplied from four regional warehouses. The supply chain director proposes closing three and serving every store from one large warehouse near Sydney. The CFO asks whether it would save money without hurting service.","clarify":[{"q":"Stock?","a":"Each warehouse holds safety stock to cover unexpected demand: $20M in total across the four."},{"q":"Holding cost?","a":"About 25% of stock value a year (capital, storage, expiry, insurance)."},{"q":"Fixed costs?","a":"Each warehouse costs about $1.5M a year to run, beyond the work of handling goods."},{"q":"Transport?","a":"Longer journeys from one site would add about $3M a year. About 15% of stores are more than 12 hours' drive from Sydney."}],"structure":{"root":"Should Coral consolidate to one warehouse?","branches":[{"head":"Inventory","items":["Safety stock needed in one place vs four"]},{"head":"Fixed costs","items":["Three warehouses closed"]},{"head":"Transport","items":["Longer distances"]},{"head":"Service","items":["Next-day delivery for distant stores"]}]},"hypothesis":"Pooling stock in one place needs less safety stock, because highs in one region offset lows in another. That saving, plus fewer sites, might outweigh extra transport, but distant stores could suffer.","questions":[{"q":"How much safety stock would one warehouse need?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>A common rule of thumb (the square-root law): if demand in each region is similar and independent, safety stock falls with the square root of the number of sites. Four sites into one: $20M ÷ √4 = <b>$10M</b>.</p> <p>Saving: $10M × 25% = <b>$2.5M a year</b>.</p>","note":"Demand in different regions partly cancels out when pooled."},{"q":"What is the net saving?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"372.76pt\" height=\"195.16pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 372.76 195.16\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 195.16 L 372.76 195.16 L 372.76 0 L 0 0 L 0 195.16 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 19.6 160.16 L 365.56 160.16 L 365.56 10.472 L 19.6 10.472 L 19.6 160.16 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"61.534545\" y=\"160.16\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(44.158295 175.36) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-26\" d=\"M 2176 0 L 384 0 L 384 448 L 1011 448 L 1011 4019 L 384 4019 L 384 4467 L 2176 4467 L 2176 4019 L 1549 4019 L 1549 448 L 2176 448 L 2176 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-11\" d=\"M 1056 0 L 544 0 L 544 3302 L 1056 3302 L 1056 2765 L 1082 2765 Q 1203 3046 1424 3212 Q 1645 3379 2016 3379 Q 2528 3379 2825 3049 Q 3123 2720 3123 2118 L 3123 0 L 2611 0 L 2611 2029 Q 2611 2470 2422 2694 Q 2234 2918 1862 2918 Q 1658 2918 1472 2851 Q 1286 2784 1171 2643 Q 1056 2502 1056 2291 L 1056 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-19\" d=\"M 1869 0 L 1274 0 L 115 3302 L 627 3302 L 1203 1664 L 1562 538 L 1594 538 L 1952 1664 L 2541 3302 L 3034 3302 L 1869 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" d=\"M 1786 -77 Q 1338 -77 1005 137 Q 672 352 486 739 Q 301 1126 301 1651 Q 301 2176 486 2563 Q 672 2950 1005 3164 Q 1338 3379 1786 3379 Q 2227 3379 2547 3171 Q 2867 2963 30