" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(317.73733 76.497143) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-38\" transform=\"translate(87.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p756e895aa5\"><rect x=\"19.6\" y=\"10.472\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Yearly effect ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Inventory $2.5M + fixed costs of three warehouses (3 × $1.5M = $4.5M) = $7.0M gross saving, less extra transport $3.0M = <b>$4.0M a year</b>.</p>"},{"q":"What would worry you?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li><b>Service:</b> the 15% of stores more than 12 hours away would lose next-day delivery; prescriptions can't wait. Keep a small cross-dock or use overnight carriers there.</li> <li><b>Resilience:</b> one site means one point of failure (fire, flood, strike)</li><li><b>Transition:</b> moving stock without gaps on shelves</li></ul>"}],"reco":"Consolidate, but keep a small hub for distant stores. One warehouse needs about half the safety stock ($10M instead of $20M), saving about $2.5M a year, and closing three sites saves $4.5M; after $3M of extra transport, the net saving is about $4.0M a year. The 15% of stores more than 12 hours from Sydney would lose next-day delivery, so serve them through a cross-dock or overnight carrier. Risk: one site is a single point of failure, so agree a backup site. Next step: model delivery times store by store.","great":["Applies risk pooling (square-root law) with its assumptions","Nets inventory and fixed savings against transport","Protects service for distant stores","Raises resilience"],"id":88,"slug":"coral-pharmacy"}